Activity 5 - Written Questions

1. What do all the methods (move(), special_move(), use()) in the previous activities have in common?
All the methods have the same purpose of performing an action but they act differently depending on the object that calls them, They demonstrate polymorphism because the same method name can have different implementations.

2. How does this activity show polymorphism in a gaming context?
The activity shows polymorphism by allowing different game characters and items to perform different actions using the same method name.

3. Can you think of other examples where the same action behaves differently depending on the character or item?
Yes. A character's attack() method can behave differently depending on the character. A Warrior can attack with a sword, a Mage can attack with magic, and an Archer can attack with arrows.
